course/modules/FC/FC1/project.html:161:          <dd><code>instruments.py</code> at the root of your repository, with these names. <code>Bond(face_cents, coupon_bps, periods)</code> with a method <code>events()</code>, which returns a list of <code>(period, amount_cents)</code> pairs sorted by period. <code>bond_price_cents(bond, yield_bps)</code>, which returns the present value of the bond's events as an int. <code>CashTrade(quantity, price_cents, side, settlement_day)</code> with a method <code>events()</code>, which returns the one settlement event of the trade. Start from <a href="grader/starter.py">the starter file</a>, whose names and signatures are complete. The module docstring holds the conventions block: the sign convention, the period indexing and the rounding rule, in your own words. Not checked by the autograder; a reviewer reads it.</dd>
course/modules/FC/FC1/project.html:163:          <dd>Standard library only (not checked by the autograder; a reviewer reads it). Money is an int in cents at every output: a coupon or a price is computed from exact fractions and rounded once, to the nearest cent with a half going away from zero, and a trade amount is an exact integer product. Each named condition below raises <code>ValueError</code>. Any other invalid input may raise any exception or return. On the inputs the suite checks for silence (the seeded case, the valid boundaries and the named refusals it lists), no function prints or warns.
